{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/862091-how-to-keep-high-resources-hunters-from-breaking-themes","id":862091,"title":"How to keep High Resources Hunters, from breaking themes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-08T12:41:46-07:00","id":862091,"title":"How to keep High Resources Hunters, from breaking themes?","content":"Somethings bothered me for a while.. Hunters, Hunters Hunted II in Particular, how to keep a char with resources 5 from upsetting a theme for a project Twilight game in particular of &quot;were underfunded and under equiped, and viewed as a laughing stock by the rest of the Bureau","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T14:08:07-07:00","id":862177,"title":"","content":"You tell the player that the character doesn't fit the theme of the game you are trying to run and have him change it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T15:32:11-07:00","id":862216,"title":"","content":"How is a high resources character maintaining high Resources if their employed by an underfunded agency?<br /> <br /> Also, one millionaire does not a well funded organization make.<br /> <br /> Beyond things like single investigations easily costing hundreds of thousand dollars - which would drain such wealth quickly - most federal agencies have strong rules regarding spending personal money on work. Law enforcement agents can't spend money to send samples to private labs so they'll get processed faster; it creates the appearance of tampering even if there is none.<br /> <br /> It seems like you can juggle that fairly easily: Resources can't be used heavily in an &quot;official&quot; context. And you can have other agents resent the PC(s) since one of them is rich on the side; without the ability to fund the agency as a whole, so it all just makes the PC(s) lives easier while everyone else is stuck in the mud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T19:12:33-07:00","id":862356,"title":"","content":"How does the fbi agent have resources 5?<br /> <br /> High spending is going to bring high attention which creates its own problems. Besides various supernatural conspiracies with their own financial-mojo whose attention you might bring, it also is going to raise a lot of questions in the Bureau.<br /> <br /> I mean, I wouldn't screw over the player if they invested character points in &quot;I'm a hereditary billionaire, but my parents were killed so I dedicated my life to law enforcement&quot; - but if they really go wild with spending on the hunt, I'd eventually have &quot;investigations&quot; freeze their assets as a plot point once the Camarilla, Technocracy, Pentex, Glass Walkers, or whoever gets annoyed with them (and give the player the liquidated xp from the background to spend elsewhere).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-30-2016, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T04:28:57-07:00","id":862545,"title":"","content":"Valid point, and some infiltrator could pin him as a lynchpin that needs &quot;removed&quot; so the rest of a problematic investigation will collapse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:52:38-07:00","id":863034,"title":"","content":"You could pit them against equally wealthy enemies. You can't just &quot;disappear&quot; someone with their own team of flesh-eating lawyers on speed dial, and who have round-the-clock surveillance and security. Opposing them requires subtlety and skill - think &quot;James Bond&quot; or &quot;Thomas Crown&quot;, not street justice.<br /> <br /> Alternately, pit them against enemies where wealth is worthless. There's nothing to buy in the sewers, after all. And a powerful monster that has no social presence, and only emerges to feed, will quickly make the player wish they'd stocked up on combat skills, not cash.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Do keep in mind, though, that the player has paid to have a wealthy character, the same way another player might have stocked up on psychic powers, or contacts, or . . . So you need to give them a chance to shine, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 04-10-2016, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T02:09:03-07:00","id":863082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/862091-how-to-keep-high-resources-hunters-from-breaking-themes#post862091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somethings bothered me for a while.. Hunters, Hunters Hunted II in Particular, how to keep a char with resources 5 from upsetting a theme for a project Twilight game in particular of &quot;were underfunded and under equiped, and viewed as a laughing stock by the rest of the Bureau</div> </div> </div> </div>Discuss things with the player and come to a consensus is pretty much the only answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:00:31-07:00","id":875227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/862091-how-to-keep-high-resources-hunters-from-breaking-themes?p=862177#post862177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You tell the player that the character doesn't fit the theme of the game you are trying to run and have him change it</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The ST/DM is the one who sets how far up someone can buy backrounds and skills etc. He could simply say &quot;sorry, Resources 5, is not allowed.. Spend points elsewhere&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T16:57:56-07:00","id":909597,"title":"","content":"Fair points, another thing on government hunters wanted to ask, with them being so poorly funded and understaffed, think its reasonable, for them to work with civilian monster hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:12:34-07:00","id":909663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/862091-how-to-keep-high-resources-hunters-from-breaking-themes?p=909597#post909597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair points, another thing on government hunters wanted to ask, with them being so poorly funded and understaffed, think its reasonable, for them to work with civilian monster hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do the feds endanger regular civilians to arrest criminals? No, why would government hunter teams endanger the very people they are paid to protect by letting them get involved in a government investigation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:37:13-07:00","id":909686,"title":"","content":"Your on a slippery slope assuming the Government hunters, are more aimed at protecting the public then at flouting the collective penis of their agency<br /> <br /> now that COULD be another reason not to accept aid from outsiders<br /> <br /> but showing that &quot;Americans united as one&quot; Could also be how some jingoistic Hunters would see it<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T18:45:04-07:00","id":909695,"title":"","content":"What's with your hard on for jingoistic npc's? Seriously? It's not world of darkness tumblr....<br /> <br /> Why would a top secret branch of the FBI who's sole purpose is to hunt things man doesn't need to know about flaunt any sort of jurisdictional power over people just for personal reasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:09:01-07:00","id":909713,"title":"","content":"Im not sure, but I'll say this much, I was hoping to expatriate, before my MS diagnosis last year.<br /> <br /> point, but in the project twilight book (Which I just finally bought at start of this month got a POD of it) it gives the impression that that their focused as much on getting information as on protecting the people. specificly with the aim of &quot;Curbing, or even controlling, the supernatural&quot; <br /> <br /> Was suggesting that thing with working with civilian hunters idea, in case ST's want an excuse to incorporate hunters with different agenda's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:30:02-07:00","id":909733,"title":"","content":"Why would individual hunters who are already paranoid and clickish want to work with the government who plans on controlling what they seek to remove from the face of the earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:43:23-07:00","id":909752,"title":"","content":"well the civilian hunters dont know that, most government hunters PROBALY dont know it, like in season 4 of buffy, most of the &quot;Initiative&quot; had NO IDEA, they were involved with plans to WEAPONIZE demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:46:00-07:00","id":909756,"title":"","content":"Again why would paranoid hunters want to work with a government that for all they know is compromised and being controlled by the very forces they want to eliminate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:31:22-07:00","id":910247,"title":"","content":"Regarding civilian hunters interactions with the government agency tasked with investigating and dealing with the supernatural (hereafter referred to as the agency) generally would not want to work with civilians, or even have them aware of what they are dealing with. Generally civilian hunters would be viewed as dangerous variables at best or domestic terrorists (probably even supernaturals) at worst. If they did run into a civilian hunter I see a few things happening assuming the civilian hunter wasnt killed during the initial meeting.<ul><li>The civilian hunter is going to be brought in for questioning (especially focusing on where they got their supernatural information and any weaponry they had).</li> <li>Any weapons the civilian hunter had will be checked for legality.</li> <li>A background check will be run on the civilian hunter not only to get personal information but to check for any warrants, arrests, or other legal issues.</li> <li>The civilian hunter will probably be held for at least the day if not longer (assuming the previous background check came clean and the weapons are legal) while the agency determines the best course of action.</li> <li>Edit [If the above come out clean A will probably happen. If there are problems or suspicions B will occur] A) If funding allows the and the civilian hunter acquitted themselves with the proper propriety they might offered a job working for the government, otherwise the agency will most likely tell the hunter to stop what they are doing with a warning that if they continue the next time they cross paths the agency will not be so lenient in a civilian interfering with a governmental investigation (something along the lines of &quot;While we appreciate the desire to protect yourself and others we cannot have civilians endangering themselves or others with reckless actions. If this happens again we will prosecute you to the fullest extent of the law.&quot;). The agency will then probably continue to do some monitoring of the civilian to insure compliance with their request and to check for supernatural connection. B) Something came up illegal or suspicious, and the agency will establish cause to continue to hold the hunter and either begin normal legal prosecution (using everything applicable with no legal infraction being too small to use after all they got Al Capone on tax evasion) or use various anti terror measures to hold the civilian hunter as long as possible while they being investigating them more in depth.</li> </ul><br /> No matter what I do not see the agency condoning civilian hunters attempting to deal with the supernatural, the chance for death or corruption are simply too high, the stakes too great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","user":"Cynic01","date":".  Edited for clarity 06-08-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:31:01-07:00","id":911101,"title":"","content":"Fair points, but at this point &quot;Desperate times breed desperate measures&quot; <br /> <br /> youve made a good point though.<br /> <br /> Thinking how to incorporate, a government hunter into a mixed cell... one idea, is he's an infiltrator there to see what all these monster hunters are up to, should they be coopted, steered a certain way, or rounded up and arrested.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question barely related at all, the Mentor background, how to keep it working as a pro, not a con, when you play sabbat, unseelie, or such.<br /> <br /> Played an Ailil sidhe once, asked her mentor to inform their house of how she was geased by a Dougal Baron.<br /> <br /> he agreed to do so, but had to wonder, is that inappropiate to ask your mentor to essentialy run errands for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:12:33-07:00","id":911222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/862091-how-to-keep-high-resources-hunters-from-breaking-themes?p=911101#post911101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question barely related at all, the Mentor background, how to keep it working as a pro, not a con, when you play sabbat, unseelie, or such.<br /> <br /> Played an Ailil sidhe once, asked her mentor to inform their house of how she was geased by a Dougal Baron.<br /> he agreed to do so, but had to wonder, is that inappropiate to ask your mentor to essentialy run errands for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to your first question, can you specify what you mean by working as a pro instead of a con?<br /> <br /> As for the second that's up to the ST what the mentor is willing to do. Tasks they might not agree to do (but aren't flat out) have the player roll one of the player's social attributes (based on how they were asking for the mentor's help) + mentor rating; with a difficulty based on the task itself (generally how dangerous) on a success the mentor agrees to the task, failure the mentor denies the request (perhaps saying something along the lines of, &quot;I thought you were further along than this, you shouldn't need me to do this.&quot;, on a botch the request has angered the mentor (possibly even consider lowering the mentor rating or losing it entirely if the character has angered the mentor before). If the mentor does agree to a task 'beneath' them, the mentor doesn't necessarily have to do it themselves, if its beneath them they might have other underlings/students who can do it and then the mentor simply reports the results.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T07:28:13-07:00","id":912226,"title":"","content":"Well When you play an Unseelie fae, or such they'll be more grudging about helping you, and more likely to give COMMANDS at times<br /> <br /> thats what I meant to make sure its still a pro not a con.<br /> <br /> Oh on resources in general, in the anniversary edition resources says you can live at resources 3 indefinitely wherever you are, if you have resources 5<br /> <br /> Or 1 indefinitely with resources 3<br /> <br /> Wanted to ask, hows that achieved at the various tiers, resources 1 is what, living in a motel a few nights<br /> <br /> Resources 2 and 3 are both hotels, though im not sure what kinds.<br /> <br /> Theirs only so many Truly AWESOME hotels on the planet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-11-2016, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T22:39:39-07:00","id":912651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/862091-how-to-keep-high-resources-hunters-from-breaking-themes?p=912226#post912226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well When you play an Unseelie fae, or such they'll be more grudging about helping you, and more likely to give COMMANDS at times thats what I meant to make sure its still a pro not a con.<br /> <br /> Oh on resources in general, in the anniversary edition resources says you can live at resources 3 indefinitely wherever you are, if you have resources 5 Or 1 indefinitely with resources 3<br /> Wanted to ask, hows that achieved at the various tiers, resources 1 is what, living in a motel a few nights<br /> Resources 2 and 3 are both hotels, though im not sure what kinds.<br /> Theirs only so many Truly AWESOME hotels on the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mentors of things like Unseelie fae, Sabbat vampires, and other 'antagonist' groups are not necessarily grudging about helping you. Rather they want to shape you into a useful apprentice or protege or may just like your character for some capricious reason. The mentor clearly sees potential in you and doesnt want to waste it and their help may less come with orders and more ask for favors and aid dealing with minor issues they dont have the time to deal with themselves, but need a trusted aide to handle. They might treat the character paternally or push them to better themselves with challenges (a mentor like the latter is more likely to phrase requests to the character as orders). Remember the mentor should be on the same side as the character, just because they are part of an &quot;evil&quot; group they are united in their cause. Where such a mentor might come off as more evil is in response to failure as they will be less forgiving especially of multiple failures, such a student could lose rating in mentor or lose the mentor altogether as the mentor no longer thinks the student is 'worth their time'. Also student who too often seeks the mentor's aid or seeks it for things they can do themselves are much more likely to irritate the mentor and run into the same problem as a constant failure, the mentor may lose interest in their student and no longer help them (something along the lines of, &quot;I have no time for dullards who cant even handle the most simple tasks on their own; I was supposed to enlighten you, not hold your hand&quot;.<br /> <br /> Each dot of resources covers a range of incomes and ownings so there I always saw some leeway as to whats available as temporary accommodations based partly on the characters other holding and assets, basically the super wealthy can live like the middle class easily for a long time even when away from 'home'. Here's what I saw as possible options for that 'temporary/indefinite' level<ul><li>Resources 1: A motel room, a hotel room, a cheap apartment, a trailer, a RV</li> <li>Resources 2: A nice hotel room, a decent apartment, a cheaper condominium, renting a small house</li> <li>Resources 3: An extravagant hotel room, a nice apartment, a condominium, buying a smaller house, renting a larger house</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T06:50:33-07:00","id":913359,"title":"","content":"An addendum on both<br /> <br /> <br /> one problem in particular on On Mentor is if your an unseelie childling it seems that the higher rrated (And thus more important) Your mentor is, the less patience he'[ll have.<br /> <br /> I think its reasonable a childlings mentor would know their not ready to stand on their own two feet yet... <br /> <br /> but would also feel that coddling them will get in the way of them EVER being able to do so, and some of the 'help' they might give might every now and then be unwelcome in the sense of forcing them to learn and grow<br /> <br /> oh on the resources thing, any ideas how to handle it for a member of a circus a Stereotypical romani (The G words forbidden as a slur, I know the real world romani people do NOT generally live like this) A shadowlord judge of doom who roams looking for criminals against the litany to punish, silent strider or Eshu Messenger, etc.<br /> <br /> point is when your on the move most of the time is an RV most appropiate? <br /> <br /> also note I found RV's that go for $3,000,000<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:42:31-07:00","id":913406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/862091-how-to-keep-high-resources-hunters-from-breaking-themes?p=913359#post913359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh on the resources thing, any ideas how to handle it for a member of a circus a Stereotypical romani (The G words forbidden as a slur, I know the real world romani people do NOT generally live like this) A shadowlord judge of doom who roams looking for criminals against the litany to punish, silent strider or Eshu Messenger, etc. point is when your on the move most of the time is an RV most appropiate? also note I found RV's that go for $3,000,000</div> </div> </div> </div>While an RV might not always be most appropriate, because of the range of prices and qualities a RV is always a possible option. Famous music stars and some of their tour buses or hotels they stay in are good examples of 4 or 5 resources characters and what the 'indefinite' level is while traveling. Without knowing the resource ratings of the examples you are asking about I can only guess but here are my thoughts (with a guessed permanent/temporary resource rating) on what they might do while traveling<ul><li>Circus member (1/None) Normal accommodations are either provided by the circus or they own an RV/Mobile Home. When traveling away from the circus, they arent making any money and would either be using their RV/Mobile Home or spending their small amount of extra cash on a cheap motel and wont be able to stay long maybe a week, up to a month at best and the character would then not have any 'extra' cash on hand for awhile after.</li> <li>Shadowlord Judge of Doom (3/1) Considering the political nature of Shadowlords I generally assume they have a higher average resource rating than most other tribes with the exception of maybe Silver Fangs and Glass Walkers. When the Judge is traveling (which is often) they would use whatever would be most appropriate for the area where their next target is; so if in the city the Judge would get a hotel room, if the target was in the wilds the Judge might rent a RV and 'camp' in the woods, if the Judge was invited to an area to hunt someone the group that invited them might provide lodging.</li> <li>Silent Strider (1/None) Depending on how they travel the Silent Strider might very well just shift into lupus form and just find a spot to sleep like any other canine would (areas protected by trees or rocks while in the woods, public garages or subways in the city).</li> <li>Eshu Messenger (2/1[six months]) Eshu are reknowned for their wanderlust you could make an argument they would be more likely to own an RV/Mobile Home as their normal accommodations and thus only use that six month period when they choose to go somewhere they can't drive to probably staying at a hotel when they do. Depending on their status as a messenger it's possible the Eshu could include payment for lodging as part of their fee for being a messenger (so if hired by a Sidhe they may end up staying in a 5 star hotel, while if they are hired by a redcap they might get enough to barely cover a cheap motel).</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:22:22-07:00","id":946214,"title":"","content":"oh a theme I noticed in both Hunters Hunted II<br /> <br /> and Promethean the created 2nd edition<br /> <br /> in both very different games, permanent Alchemy, is Categorically impossible.<br /> <br /> why?<br /> <br /> Best Guess is fear we'd see gold become as common a copper otherwise, but I think that permanent Alchemy should be possible if difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 08-08-2016, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:20:52-07:00","id":946306,"title":"","content":"Government agents should have a minimum of Resources 2 (V20), just to reflect their benefits, salary, etc. Resources 5 (V20) would be rather uncomfortable for a hunter because people are paying attention to you. Resources 4 (V20) would be the maximum level that I would allow any PC but, even at that level, the PC would be part of the FBI because they have non-economic motivations to pursue their FBI career.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:03:51-07:00","id":947183,"title":"","content":"To quote the late Robert E. Howard:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Money and muscle, that\u2019s what I want; to be able to do any damned thing I want and get away with it. Money won\u2019t do that altogether, because if a man is a weakling, all the money in the world won\u2019t enable him to soak an enemy himself; on the other hand, unless he has money he may not be able to get away with it.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So in other words, all the money in the world won't stop a Gangrel from ripping your head off. A player is very strong in one field? Challenge him in another. Basic Storyteller trick.<br /> <br /> Also, it sesms that Robert E. Howard was so badass he didn't soak damage, he soaked entire enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:50:14-07:00","id":968247,"title":"","content":"Oh another question on government monster hunters?<br /> <br /> an idea I have for my current game, while it would work on the surface im asking some advise to make sure I understand the full impact of it<br /> <br /> a group of NPC FBI agents only one is affiliated with the SAD the rest are CLUELESS to the supernatural etc.<br /> <br /> Ideas on the impact beyond them having no defense from the delerium training with Numina. and likely carrying no silver ammo.<br /> <br /> Anything else<br /> <br /> thinking how to keep in mind hes constantly steering the other Agents where he wants them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img i